    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Say which process you are in — every turn",
      "prov:value": "**Say which permission you are acting under.** Entering a task in a lane\nmeans performing it as that lane's role, and since issue #1180 that needs an\nODRL rule that permits it there (`permits()` in `schemas/content/odrl.ts`: the actor,\nthe action, and the process, task and role as scope). If the answer is\n`unknown` or `deny`, you are out of process for that task: route it to a lane\nwhose actor holds the permission, or stop and ask. The engine enforces this\nbefore the task at the deterministic end of the spectrum; at the agentic end\nnothing stops you, and the QA/QC report over the PROV-O record finds it\nafterwards (`agentic-harness.html#bpmn-execution`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1180"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming it is not the same as recording it (advisory)",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-09-20, bean `vlhk`.** 54 proposals merged in one four-hour\nwindow, and `beans/workflows/` — the declared `workflow-state` graph — held\nonly `.gitkeep`. **Not one session recorded a running instance.** A reviewer\nsweeping that window could not classify a single session by lane, which is the\none thing this section exists to make possible. `supn` and `v49e` measured the\nsame empty directory from other angles.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vlhk",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming it is not the same as recording it (advisory)",
      "prov:value": "There were two readings — the processes are not being run, or they are run and\nthe state is not committed — and they call for opposite remedies. The owner\nsettled it, 2026-09-20: **the processes are real, and the instance is\nrecorded.** So:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming it is not the same as recording it (advisory)",
      "prov:value": "**This rule is ADVISORY: nothing gates on it.** Bean `5ulq` measured the\nremedy above on 2026-10-02: 9 instances against 755 merges since the ruling,\nand no CI workflow reading the graph. That is the `xom7` shape, a STRICT rule\nwhose breach looks exactly like compliance. Calling it STRICT taught readers\nthat the word is decoration, including where it is enforced. Offered the\nchoice between gating it, making it advisory, or scrapping it, the owner ruled\non 2026-10-10: **make it advisory.** So record the instance when the turn is\nin a process, but no check refuses a merge without one, and none should be\nadded without a new ruling.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5ulq",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-10"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming it is not the same as recording it (advisory)",
      "prov:value": "**The gap is computed, never quoted.** `vlhk`'s 54 went stale by ~14× in two\nweeks with nothing to say so. `bun run cat workflow:instances` prints today's\ncount: instances recorded, instances started since the ruling, first-parent\nmerges in the same window, and the CI workflows that read the graph. Merges\nare an upper bound on the instances owed, since a steward's train, a docs-only\nfix or a revert may have none. The command reports the gap and exits 0; only\na count it cannot make (store unmounted, shallow clone, an undatable\ninstance) exits 2."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Arriving without the sweep — a mid-session clone, a project thread",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-10-30, the \"Fix wonky minimap\" thread.** A project thread\nstarted with no repository. It cloned smart-ra, the tools layer and the\ncontent core mid-session, fixed and merged\nhttps://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/pull/1025,\nand repinned smart-ra. It never named a process, never loaded\n`delivery-summary` or `staging-review`, and gave its first result with no\nstaging link. Every route to this skill was closed:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "pull/1025",
        "2026-10-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Arriving without the sweep — a mid-session clone, a project thread",
      "prov:value": "When the brief is written **during a live discussion with a person**, it also\nnames the discussion: who is talking with the person, how to reach them, the\nstanding card rules, and any feedback channel in play (a review sheet's id and\ntab, an issue). That is `definitions.discussion` of the\n[`hand-back-to-discussion`](../../conduct/conduct-core/hand-back-to-discussion.md)\ninput schema, and it is what lets the thread hand its cards, questions and\nresults back instead of leaving them in its own channel (owner, 2026-10-31,\ncat-harness#861).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "cat-harness#861",
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What you MOVED while you were out of process",
      "prov:value": "**The only possible record is what was written to a bean at the time.** That is\nnot a convention this skill is adding; it is the consequence of two decisions\ntaken elsewhere. Beans carry **no anchor** (owner's rule, 2026-09-19): a bean\nis not a thing pinned to a block, it is the record that a pinning *changed*.\nAnd `workflow/bean-link.ts` already has the `note` op that writes it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What you MOVED while you were out of process",
      "prov:value": "**Considered and rejected: giving the note its own history.** A `movedFrom`\nfield would make a move self-documenting and remove the need for any of this.\nIt was not taken, because the history then lives in the artefact being moved —\nso a note deleted, or moved by a tool that does not maintain the field, takes\nits own audit trail with it. The bean is a *separate* record, which is what an\naudit trail has to be."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/process-state.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Worked example — reading a bean back as the trail",
      "prov:value": "Bean `5oai`, 2026-09-19, is one, and the episode is an agent's rather than a\nsticky's — which is the point: the mechanism does not care what moved.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5oai",
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    }
  ]
